/**

@page page_exahype_faq FAQ and troubleshooting

# Large generated records exhaust the thread stack

High polynomial orders and large patches can make the per-cell call record too
large for a thread stack. A debugger typically reports the failure while it
constructs a local array of the generated cell type.

Use a smaller patch or order, or select a heap-based storage scheme. A
heap-based record keeps only its small owning handle in the traversal call
block while the patch payload remains in heap storage.

*/
